- ### Parsing
+ ### Analyse

- `Parser.parse` reads Markdown text into a document, which is a `Markdown of Layout`:
+ `Parser.parse` lit un texte Markdown en un document, qui est un `Markdown of Layout` :

= `Parser.parse` reads Markdown text into a document, which is a `Markdown of Layout`:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val document = Parser.parse(t"# Title\n\nSome **bold** text.")
+ val document = Parser.parse(t"# Title\n\nSome **bold** text.")

= val document = Parser.parse(t"# Title\n\nSome **bold** text.")
- ```
+ ```

- Markdown is also parsed incrementally, from a [stream](streams.md), reading lines as they
- arrive, without holding the source. Only the tree is retained, and the raw text of each
- paragraph, which is parsed later. A long document is therefore parsed without ever being
- held whole:
+ Markdown s'analyse aussi de façon incrémentale, à partir d'un [flux](streams.md), en lisant les
+ lignes au fur et à mesure qu'elles arrivent, sans conserver la source. Seuls l'arbre et le
+ texte brut de chaque paragraphe, analysé plus tard, sont conservés. Un long document s'analyse
+ donc sans jamais être conservé en entier :

= held whole:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- import dysasymptotics.linearSize
+ import dysasymptotics.linearSize

- val readme = t"# Readme\n\nThe first paragraph.\n\nThe second."
+ val readme = t"# Readme\n\nThe first paragraph.\n\nThe second."

= val readme = t"# Readme\n\nThe first paragraph.\n\nThe second."
- ```
+ ```

= val readme = t"# Readme\n\nThe first paragraph.\n\nThe second."
= ```
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= val readme = t"# Readme\n\nThe first paragraph.\n\nThe second."
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= val readme = t"# Readme\n\nThe first paragraph.\n\nThe second."
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
- ##
+ ##

- Out.println(Parser.parse(readme.stream).children.size.show)
+ Out.println(Parser.parse(readme.stream).children.size.show)

- Out.println(readme.read[Markdown of Layout].children.size.show)
+ Out.println(readme.read[Markdown of Layout].children.size.show)

= Out.println(readme.read[Markdown of Layout].children.size.show)
- ```
+ ```

- The whole CommonMark conformance suite passes through the streaming entry, a character at a
- time, so a document which is split at any point parses to the same tree as the whole text.
+ Toute la suite de conformité de CommonMark passe par le point d'entrée en flux, un caractère à
+ la fois : un document découpé en n'importe quel point s'analyse donc en le même arbre que le
+ texte entier.

- ### Rendering to HTML
+ ### Rendu en HTML

- `html` converts a parsed document to HTML, and `show` writes the result as text. A document
- of blocks becomes flow content, and the inline content within it becomes phrasing content,
- so the output is well-formed by construction:
+ `html` convertit un document analysé en HTML, et `show` écrit le résultat sous forme de texte.
+ Un document de blocs devient du contenu de flux, et le contenu en ligne qu'il contient devient
+ du contenu phrasé : la sortie est donc bien formée par construction :

= so the output is well-formed by construction:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= so the output is well-formed by construction:
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= so the output is well-formed by construction:
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
- ##
+ ##

- Out.println(document.html.show)
+ Out.println(document.html.show)

= Out.println(document.html.show)
- ```
+ ```

- ### The syntax tree
+ ### L'arbre syntaxique

- The `children` of a document are `Layout` nodes, and each has its inline content as `Prose`.
- A document can therefore be inspected, or transformed, by matching on the tree:
+ Les `children` d'un document sont des nœuds `Layout`, et chacun a son contenu en ligne sous
+ forme de `Prose`. Un document peut donc être inspecté, ou transformé, par filtrage sur l'arbre :

= A document can therefore be inspected, or transformed, by matching on the tree:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val heading = document.children.head match
+ val heading = document.children.head match

-   case Layout.Heading(_, level, Prose.Textual(text)) => (level, text)
+   case Layout.Heading(_, level, Prose.Textual(text)) => (level, text)

-   case _                                             => (0, t"")
+   case _                                             => (0, t"")

=   case _                                             => (0, t"")
- ```
+ ```

=   case _                                             => (0, t"")
= ```
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

=   case _                                             => (0, t"")
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

=   case _                                             => (0, t"")
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
- ##
+ ##

- Out.println(heading.inspect)
+ Out.println(heading.inspect)

= Out.println(heading.inspect)
- ```
+ ```

